# The release artifact is THIS directory: `git archive HEAD:plugin`, so a rule
# that must hold for the artifact has to live here — an archive of a subtree
# reads the .gitattributes files inside that subtree, and never sees the one at
# the repository root. Both rules below are therefore this directory's own:
#
#   src/            the TypeScript the .js are made from. The artifact ships the
#                   emitted modules (a client's own node cannot strip types), and
#                   each of them names its source in its banner, so the sources
#                   are dev material: `git archive HEAD:plugin` is
#                   component.json + index.js + the three modules it requires.
#   .gitattributes  this file, which is the rule itself and ships nowhere.
src/ export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
